\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Stopped trajectory}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{agent}

\p{If #{\tau_{\mathrm{stop}}=n}, the \newvocab{stopped trajectory} is
##{
Z=(S_0,O_0,A_0,S_1,O_1,A_1,\ldots,
A_{n-1},S_n,O_n).
}
It contains the environment states as well as the public action-observation
record. Its public projection is the history #{H_n} of \ref{ftip-0021}.}

\p{For #{n=0}, the trajectory is #{(S_0,O_0)} and contains no action. A
terminal utility may depend on the full trajectory when evaluated inside the
environment, even though the policy is restricted to its public projection.}
